5080773793200058-f292c751-3046-44d7-8044-913c25a93606"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"fd82aae16b34dacf052dcf4b899781f683a7a8ef4cadf2f3218a774f0cae18f2","event_uuid":"a976319a-79b9-45a2-bf1d-de110b9b036b","position":{"commit_sha":"020896068ffdf4201d839e7ee0bd866782101587","position":"1795081309656486033-a976319a-79b9-45a2-bf1d-de110b9b036b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"619623674b4f4e828a690f34e93f3d783bbd4239664ac5eb86e946c586d9dcba","event_uuid":"e1c6d6b4-b6a8-43bf-9a31-4beeb5992595","position":{"commit_sha":"2e83d01d5200b5a133b87d697155c89acf689382","position":"1795081321444094806-e1c6d6b4-b6a8-43bf-9a31-4beeb5992595"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stopped on a policy decision; handing back. The diagnosis in the description stands: ad49f17f is the review bot's clone, eea68b7f is the MCP server, b2b5c498 is the retired pre-migration clone, and all are real overlaps. The plan review (BLOCK, 2026-11-18) found 2 facts that change the fix:\n\n1. The detector groups spans by event `author`, which is git `user.name` (`_seam.author()`), not by rebar identity. The remedy I proposed, `rebar identity create/use`, changes only `author_id`, so it would not stop new overlaps. The working lever for a shared service account is a distinct git `user.name` in one clone.\n2. Each (env, author) span is the min..max of all history (`fsck_authorship._widen`), and the row is counted (`fsck_tracker_health.py:53`). So even after a remedy, the 2026-08-26 migration overlap (b2b5c498) and the months of shared \"Rebar Bot\" history (ad49f17f) keep the server's fsck at exit 1 permanently. No message wording changes that.\n\n**Decision: should a finished, historical overlap keep failing fsck forever?**\n- Today: server fsck exits 1 on every run because of this row.\n- Event history is never rewritten, so whole-history spans can only grow.\n- The review bot and MCP server both commit as \"Rebar Bot\" by deployment design.\n\nHow should ENV_ID_MISMATCH treat it?\n(1) Keep it counted and fix only the message: name each foreign id with its author and last overlap time, and give the correct remedy (a distinct git `user.name` per long-lived clone). The server's fsck stays at exit 1 permanently.\n**(2) Count only overlaps still live, meaning the foreign env wrote within a fixed window of the current env's latest event (a code constant, no config key), and report finished overlaps as an uncounted note. Also give the review bot its own git `user.name` in infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, landed by normal autodeploy. After the window passes, the server's fsck exits 0.**\n(3) Do (2) without the deployment change: the ad49f17f row stays counted until someone changes the review bot's author name.","timestamp":1795028400223094024},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Operator decision (2026-11-18): detect environments by signing key, not by author\n\nRejected: creating a new identity (a distinct git user.name or author per clone); fsck failing permanently; counting finished overlaps indefinitely.\n\nOperator's model: each environment has its own signing identity, even when the author is the same. Checkouts in the same environment may share that key.\n\nResulting rule for ENV_ID_MISMATCH:\n- Several env ids signed by one key are checkouts in the same environment. Not reported.\n- Env ids signed by different keys are different environments. Not reported.\n- One env id whose events are signed by 2 or more keys during overlapping periods is reported: a checkout's .env-id carried into another environment. A sequential change (key rotation) is not reported.\n- No author grouping, no time window, no new identity, no config key.\n\nMeasured on origin/tickets, last 1,500 commits, using the key fingerprint embedded in each event's author_sig SSHSIG:\n- eea68b7f (server): key biqEFL9T\u2026 on 1,137 events, plus 1 event signed with YWib9Gj1\u2026.\n- ad49f17f: key oGCqzgfD\u2026 on 311 events. Mostly LINK, python-channel CREATE and REVIEW_RESULT events. Mapped earlier to the review bot's clone at /var/gerrit/site/reviewbot-tickets.\n- 492a5c71 (the operator's Mac checkout, from its .env-id): key oGCqzgfD\u2026 on 223 events.\n\nOpen points for the implementer to check first:\n1. ad49f17f and the Mac checkout share key oGCqzgfD\u2026. If ad49f17f is on the server box, then 2 environments share one key, which contradicts the operator's model. Confirm where ad49f17f lives (read-only), and file a separate bug if the key was copied across environments. Do not change keys or deployments; stop and report.\n2. The one eea68b7f event signed with YWib9Gj1\u2026: determine whether it is a rotation, a different signer, or an anomaly. Under the new rule it would be reported if it overlaps the main key's span.\n3. Some events carry no parseable author_sig (KeyError in the sample: 36 on eea68b7f, 29 on 492a5c71). Define how unsigned events are treated, without making them a false-positive source.","timestamp":1795038638977466271},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation notes (2026-11-18 PST)\n\n- Decision (in scope): `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` is report-only (`counted: false`). Key spans cover all history and events are never rewritten, so a counted overlap could never stop counting without a time window; the operator rejected both permanent failure and a window.\n- Open point 1 (shared key): filed `unaroused-destitute-cobra`. The Mac's `identity.signing_key` fingerprint prefix is `oGCqzgfDMp`, comment `rebar-bot \u2026 rotated-20260907`, the same key the review bot's clone `ad49f17f` has signed with since 2026-09-07 18:05. No key or deployment changed.\n- Open point 2: the `YWib9Gj1qZ` key on `eea68b7f` covers 2026-08-26 09:50 to 2026-09-07 15:38, and `biqEFL9T96` starts 2026-09-15. That is a rotation, and it is not reported.\n- Open point 3: unsigned events, unparseable signatures and unstamped events add no key span.\n- AC 3 (live run): ran the new tally and detector read-only over the Mac's tracker at `eed5d616a6c` (equal to `origin/tickets`). It read 143,869 live events and found 26 (env, key) pairs. `divergence_report` returned None, so no `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` line. Key parsing added no measurable time: 33.8 s with it, 35.1 s with it stubbed out (file I/O dominates).\n- Portability: pure bytes/string/base64/hashlib code, no process, filesystem-semantics or signal API.","timestamp":1795069181098052318},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3448 merged as 5d3641f233ee756bc030f92b491dc59c2594c56b (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, CI run 44491334716). Local make verify passed on a0a2a9a802a: 21,446 passed plus 226 integration. The first verify failed only because the new helper's name matched the retired-HMAC name scan in `tests/unit/test_hmac_retirement.py`; renamed to `signer_key_id`. No Windows sweep is needed: pure string/bytes logic with no subprocess, fd, path, encoding or permission change.","timestamp":1795080652473180116}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793789721264666001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"39377bc8-b435-4289-ad20-763e35109e94","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"bbd4-cec2-ecdb-46d9"},{"link_uuid":"0368b1a9-963e-40eb-aea3-38ce330cbef1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f0f0-9cf9-6c7e-4bf4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe MCP server's `rebar fsck` reports `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` for its own environment `eea68b7f` against `ad49f17f` (the review bot's clone) and `b2b5c498` (the retired pre-migration clone), and counts it, so fsck exits 1 on every run. The detector, `divergence_report` (`src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py:250`), groups event time spans by event `author` (git `user.name`, collected by `EnvAuthorshipTally.observe` in `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py`). The review bot and the MCP server both commit as \"Rebar Bot\" by design, so their spans overlap and the line fires permanently.\n\nOperator decision (comment, 2026-11-18): detect environments by signing key, not author. Each environment has its own signing key even when the author is the same; checkouts in one environment may share a key. Rejected: creating a new identity, fsck failing permanently, counting finished overlaps indefinitely. No author grouping, no time window, no config key.\n\n## Findings (read-only, 2026-11-18 PST)\nProbe over every live (non-retired, non-SNAPSHOT) event in the Mac's tracker, which matches `origin/tickets` (0/0), reading the key embedded in each event's `author_sig` SSHSIG:\n- `eea68b7f` (MCP server): key `YWib9Gj1qZ` 2026-08-26 09:50 to 2026-09-07 15:38, then key `biqEFL9T96` 2026-09-15 11:13 to 2026-11-18 21:46. Sequential: a rotation. The \"1 event signed with YWib\" in the earlier 1,500-commit sample is the tail of the first key's era.\n- `ad49f17f` (review bot): key `PU4nHIqJCR` to 2026-09-07 15:49, then `oGCqzgfDMp` from 2026-09-07 18:05. Sequential.\n- `reconciler` env: `PU4nHIqJCR` then `oGCqzgfDMp`, sequential. Every other env id has one key.\n- So under the key rule, the live store has no `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` row.\n- Open point 1: `oGCqzgfDMp` (comment `rebar-bot \u2026 rotated-20260907`) is both the review bot's key and the Mac's configured `identity.signing_key`. Two environments share one key. Filed as `unaroused-destitute-cobra`; no key or deployment changed here. Effect on this rule: a `.env-id` carried between those two would not be reported (a false negative, never a false positive).\n- Open point 3: unsigned events (no `author_sig`) and signatures whose key cannot be parsed carry no key, so they create no key span and cannot cause or hide a report.\n\n## Approach\n1. `EnvAuthorshipTally.observe` records, per `(env_id, key fingerprint)`, the first and last event timestamp. The key comes from `rebar.attest.dsse.decode(author_sig)` then `rebar.attest.sshsig.embedded_public_key(sig)` (both existing), and the fingerprint is `SHA256:` plus the unpadded base64 SHA-256 of the key blob, the form `ssh-keygen -l` prints. Events without a key or without an integer timestamp add nothing. The per-author spans are removed (no other consumer: `identity_spans` is read only at `fsck_tracker_health.py:44`).\n2. `divergence_report(spans)` reports each env id that has 2 or more keys whose closed time spans overlap, store-wide, naming the env id, the overlapping key fingerprints and their spans. Sequential keys (rotation) and several env ids under one key are not reported.\n3. The line stays `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` but becomes report-only: `fsck_tracker_health.py` passes `False`, and `env_id_mismatch` joins `_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:78`). Reason: spans are whole-history min..max and events are never rewritten, so a counted overlap could never stop counting without a time window, which the operator rejected along with permanent fsck failure. The message tells the operator the cause (a `.env-id` copied into another environment) and the remedy (delete `.env-id` in the copied checkout so it mints its own).\n4. Update the `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` paragraph in `docs/concurrency.md` and the module docstring.\nPortability: pure Python bytes and string handling, no filesystem, process or signal API.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py`: `divergence_report`, docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py`: key spans in the tally.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py`: report-only flag.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py`: `_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS`.\n- `docs/concurrency.md`: detector description.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_env_identity_guard.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_issue_count_29c3.py`.\n\n## Testing\nTests build `author_sig` values from synthetic SSHSIG blobs with chosen embedded keys (no `ssh-keygen` needed).\n- One env id, keys A (100..300) and B (200..400): reported, names the env id and both fingerprints; fsck exits 0 and JSON marks the item `counted: false`.\n- One env id, A (100..200) then B (300..400): not reported (rotation).\n- Two env ids, one key: not reported. Two env ids, two keys: not reported.\n- Same author \"Rebar Bot\" under two env ids with overlapping spans but different keys: not reported (the server's case).\n- Unsigned events and unparseable signatures inside another key's span: not reported.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The key-overlap rule above is implemented and covered by the cases in Testing, in `tests/interfaces/store/test_env_identity_guard.py`; `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_env_identity_guard.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_issue_count_29c3.py` passes.\n- [x] `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` is report-only: a store with an overlap makes `rebar fsck` print the line and exit 0, verified by a test.\n- [x] Run against a read-only copy of the live tracker, the new detector prints no `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` line; result recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [x] `docs/concurrency.md` describes the key-based rule.\n- [x] `make verify` passes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py","reason":"divergence_report: key-overlap rule"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py","reason":"tally records (env_id, key) spans"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py","reason":"ENV_ID_MISMATCH report-only"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"describe key-based rule"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_env_identity_guard.py","reason":"rule tests"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_issue_count_29c3.py","reason":"never-counted kinds set"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f0f0-9cf9-6c7e-4bf4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a976319a-79b9-45a2-bf1d-de110b9b036b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_id":"c4d9-7807-5c55-4b93","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Server fsck reports ENV_ID_MISMATCH for services that share one author name; detect by signing key instead","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["50500226-d602-4c09-b364-f6d1ee94ecba","dc4114ad-424d-4551-9ab8-97993e7fabb6","933c8b2a-3a76-4ac8-8cda-86703f419d1e","ba7f5dca-06b6-4262-9a72-eb97d700e238","d79d8c7e-4005-4e75-b948-ca8092ea66a1","02c2a811-4e8c-47f4-aab9-70c2db11ccc0","381a34f6-fed3-4f6c-8479-6ab8a947565a","0fc7acbe-db79-4e20-ad2a-8186d693644b","e6bf760e-56ef-4d70-ac9f-b716ab716d28","70da19ce-0b3c-4dad-98c8-3775a88133c8","0368b1a9-963e-40eb-aea3-38ce330cbef1","0108f30c-ce19-4665-81b7-19f339220dbd","1f5c1afb-08b4-4899-bb0f-a1670a1965d4","f292c751-3046-44d7-8044-913c25a93606","a976319a-79b9-45a2-bf1d-de110b9b036b","e1c6d6b4-b6a8-43bf-9a31-4beeb5992595"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795081321444094807,"uuid":"29286417-4688-4fb3-a762-e18419e730c2"}
